<title>JAPAN: Japan Oct-Dec machinery orders seen up 19.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Oct-Dec machinery orders seen up 19.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, are expected to rise a seasonally adjusted 19.3 percent in the October-December period from the previous quarter, the Economic Planning Agency said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The quarter-on-quarter percentage change outlook, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders, were as follows:</p>
<p>			  OCT-DEC	JUL-SEPT(ACTUAL)</p>
<p>   Overall		 6.7		  2.8</p>
<p>   Private		19.3		 -6.7</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			  OCT-DEC	JUL-SEPT(ACTUAL)</p>
<p>   Public		 9.7		 -9.5</p>
<p>   External	     2.7		 30.4</p>
</text>
